       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or prolonged peripheral vasodilation. Amlodipine also has a long half-life, so the effects would last.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a typical starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for frail or elderly patients, or patients with hepatic impairment\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intended, please confirm that. Tell me the clinical rationale too, and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
