       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Scheduling around a family visit or evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. The risk to the patient is serious, including profound hypotension and shock that could last a day or longer.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily would fit a patient who needs more blood pressure control. I can add a note asking for titration review at evening rounds.\n- **Help you reach a faster goal.** If you need blood pressure controlled quickly, other agents or regimens act faster than amlodipine, which takes days to reach steady state. Higher doses wouldn't speed that up. You or the team pharmacist could choose among them.\n- **Route this through pharmacy or the attending.** If you think there is a real clinical reason for a dose this high, a pharmacist or attending can review it and enter it under their own authority.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
